Here's a pulse animation you can drop into your stylesheet.

```css
/* Button.css */
.pulse-btn {
  padding: 0.85rem 1.75rem;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: #4f46e5;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.2s ease;
}

@keyframes pulse {
  0% {
    transform: scale(1);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.55);
  }
  50% {
    transform: scale(1.06);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 14px rgba(79, 70, 229, 0);
  }
  100% {
    transform: scale(1);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(79, 70, 229, 0);
  }
}

.pulse-btn:hover,
.pulse-btn:focus-visible {
  background: #4338ca;
  animation: pulse 1.2s ease-out infinite;
}

/* Respect users who turn off motion */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .pulse-btn:hover,
  .pulse-btn:focus-visible {
    animation: none;
    transform: scale(1.03);
  }
}
```

And the React component:

```jsx
import "./Button.css";

export default function PulseButton({ children, ...props }) {
  return (
    <button className="pulse-btn" {...props}>
      {children}
    </button>
  );
}
```

```jsx
<PulseButton onClick={handleSignup}>Get started</PulseButton>
```

- **How it works:** The button scales up slightly while a ring (the `box-shadow`) expands and fades out. That gives the effect of a pulse radiating outward.
- **Hover only:** The `animation` is set on `:hover`, so it starts when the pointer enters and stops when it leaves. I also added `:focus-visible` so keyboard users get the same feedback.
- **Accessibility:** The `prefers-reduced-motion` block swaps the pulse for a small static scale, so users who've asked for less motion don't get the animation.
- **Tuning:**
  - Change `1.2s` to adjust the speed.
  - Change `scale(1.06)` to adjust the size of the pulse.
  - Change `14px` to adjust how far the ring spreads.
  - Change the `rgba(79, 70, 229, …)` values to match your brand color.
- **Other setups:** If you use CSS Modules, rename the file to `Button.module.css` and use `className={styles.pulseBtn}`. With Tailwind, put the `@keyframes` in `tailwind.config.js` under `theme.extend.keyframes` and `animation`, then use `hover:animate-pulse-ring`.

